penholding. Practice movement (running the writing machine) a few minutes
without the penholder, then slip the penholder into the right hand from the
left, and practice the movement without touching the pen to the paper, still
watching the arm closely, and giving more attention to correct position and
movement than to anything else.

Are you comfortable in your seat; do your arms feel comfortable; and are you
holding the penholder lightly in the hand without pinching it? Give close
attention to these things.

In the next lesson more particular attention will be given to penholding.

